# Code owners
#
# Files that decide what runs in CI, or what runs when someone installs or builds
# Open MCT, need approval from a code owner before they reach master. This takes
# effect once "Require review from Code Owners" is on in master's branch
# protection. Without it, these lines only request a review.
#
# These files can run code on GitHub's runners or on a developer's machine. Workflows
# on master also run with a write token and secrets, which pull requests from forks
# never get. Ordinary source code is not listed: any maintainer can approve that.
#
# A later matching line overrides an earlier one, so keep the owner the same on
# every line unless that is the intent.

# CI: workflows, the scripts they run, issue and pull request templates, and this
# file itself.
/.github/ @nasa/openmct-web-admin

# Dependencies and the package registry. Install scripts run on every machine that
# installs Open MCT, and on every CI run.
/package.json @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/package-lock.json @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/.npmrc @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/.nvmrc @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/e2e/package.json @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/e2e/package-lock.json @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/src/plugins/persistence/couch/package.json @nasa/openmct-web-admin

# Build configuration.
/.webpack/ @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/tsconfig.json @nasa/openmct-web-admin

# Lint and test configuration. These are JavaScript, executed by lint and test runs.
/.eslintrc.cjs @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/e2e/.eslintrc.cjs @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/karma.conf.cjs @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/e2e/playwright-*.config.js @nasa/openmct-web-admin

# The CouchDB set-up that the e2e-couchdb CI job runs.
/src/plugins/persistence/couch/couchdb-compose.yaml @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/src/plugins/persistence/couch/setup-couchdb.sh @nasa/openmct-web-admin
/src/plugins/persistence/couch/replace-localstorage-with-couchdb-indexhtml.sh @nasa/openmct-web-admin
